{
 "about": "Общие эталоны поворота эллипсоида анизотропии (ТЗ 8.6.3; ADR 0022 §6, §9; ТД14-1): ядро — bf_core/geostat/rotation.py (tests/test_geostat_rotation.py), окно — ui/src/viz/ellipsoid/frame.ts",
 "rules": "Angles of GSLIB in degrees (TZ 8.6.3): ang1 - the azimuth of the major axis a1, clockwise from north (+Y); ang2 - its dip, negative down (the plunge p = -ang2); ang3 - the turn about a1. Normalised: ang1 = ((ang1 % 360) + 360) % 360 in [0, 360); ang2 in [-90, 90] (beyond - refused); ang3 = ((ang3 % 360) + 360) % 360, minus 360 when above 180 - in (-180, 180]. The cases hold normalised angles; `normalize` - the others.\nsin/cos of degrees d: d reduced to [0, 360) as above; exact (0, 1), (1, 0), (0, -1), (-1, 0) at 0, 90, 180, 270; otherwise sin and cos of d*(PI/180) (sinCosDegCore of viz/section/plane.ts). (s1, c1), (s2, c2), (s3, c3) - of ang1, ang2, ang3. -0 is written 0.\naxes = R of TZ 8.6.3 (a = 90 - ang1: cos a = s1, sin a = c1; b = -ang2: cos b = c2, sin b = -s2; t = ang3), its rows are the axes a1, a2, a3 in the world (X east, Y north, Z up): u1 = (c2*s1, c2*c1, s2); u2 = (-c3*c1 - s3*s2*s1, c3*s1 - s3*s2*c1, s3*c2); u3 = (s3*c1 - c3*s2*s1, -s3*s1 - c3*s2*c1, c3*c2); u3 = u1 x u2. Zero angles: (0, 1, 0), (-1, 0, 0), (0, 0, 1).\natan2d(y, x): y == 0 -> 0 for x >= 0, else 180; x == 0 -> 90 for y > 0, else -90; otherwise atan2(y, x)*(180/PI).\nback (axes -> angles; `hint` - the ang1 the window holds, in the cases the ang1 of the case): u1 of unit length; rho = hypot(u1.x, u1.y); ang2 = atan2d(u1.z, rho) (not asin: no loss near +-90). If |u1.z| <= 1 - 1e-12: ang1 = atan2d(u1.x, u1.y), +360 below 0; ang3 = atan2d(u2.z, u3.z). Otherwise the major axis is vertical, the azimuth and the turn are one rotation: ang1 = hint (normalised); ang3 = ang1 + atan2d(-u2.y, -u2.x) when u1.z > 0, atan2d(u2.y, -u2.x) - ang1 when u1.z < 0; ang3 normalised as above.\nplane (the second notation: the plane of the axes a1-a2, its normal u3): n = u3; a vertical plane (|n.z| <= 1e-12): n = -n when n.x < 0 or (n.x == 0 and n.y < 0); otherwise n = -n when n.z < 0. dip = atan2d(hypot(n.x, n.y), |n.z|); dip_direction = atan2d(n.x, n.y), +360 below 0, 0 when >= 360; a vertical plane with dip_direction >= 180 -> 0; dip < 1e-6 -> dip_direction = 0 (ADR 0021, 2). With (sd, cd) of dip and (sA, cA) of dip_direction: the strike s = (-cA, sA, 0) (the azimuth dip_direction - 90), the line of dip d = s x n = (cd*sA, cd*cA, -sd), the upper normal n = (sd*sA, sd*cA, cd). pitch = atan2d(u1.d, u1.s), +180 below 0, -180 when >= 180, and 0 when >= 180 - 1e-9: in [0, 180), from the strike towards the line of dip.\nfrom_plane (dip, dip_direction, pitch -> angles): dip in [0, 90] (beyond - refused), dip_direction mod 360, pitch mod 180; (sp, cp) of pitch; u1 = cp*s + sp*d (it looks down: u1.z <= 0), u3 = n, u2 = u3 x u1; the angles - `back` of these axes with hint = dip_direction. The same ellipsoid as the angles of the case: every axis is the same line, maybe the other way. Not given where the major axis is almost vertical (its azimuth is ill-conditioned at 1e-9).\nellipsoids: anisotropy = A = diag(1, a1/a2, a1/a3)*R (rows u1, (a1/a2)*u2, (a1/a3)*u3): h_r = |A*delta| / a1 (TZ 8.6.3; the matrix of a trend). matrix = the unit sphere -> the ellipsoid, world = centre + matrix*s: its columns are a1*u1, a2*u2, a3*u3 (matrix[i][j] = a_j * u_j[i]). ends = the ends of the three axes from the centre: a1*u1, a2*u2, a3*u3.\ndirections: the direction of a variogram with the azimuth Az and the plunge p (positive down), u = (cos p*sin Az, cos p*cos Az, -sin p) - the row u1 of the angles (Az, -p, 0).\nTolerances: axes, anisotropy, matrix (relative to the largest range), ends, directions - 1e-12; an `exact` case - bit for bit; back, plane, from_plane - 1e-9 degrees.",
 "tolerance": {
  "axes": 1e-12,
  "angles": 1e-09,
  "plane": 1e-09,
  "matrix": 1e-12
 },
